# One open PR per change

Before creating a pull request:

1. Search this repository's **open** PRs for the same title.
2. Search for another open PR whose body `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves` the same issue.
3. If either match exists, push to that branch (or stop). Do not open a sibling.

Two agents that start from the same issue will pick the same Conventional Commit title. A GitHub search at start time is a race. The oldest open PR is the one that lands. CI (`ops/check-duplicate-prs.py`) fails every newer duplicate. Close the newer PR instead of renaming it to sneak past the gate.
